Re-ran the live lp85 probe WITH the split-fallback fix (06b527ea1) in the tree. lp85 L2 still does
not bank (max_depth=1, goal_satisfiable_any=False). Induction breakdown: [0] L1 engine only 12%
accurate (world_model_accuracy_below_threshold) -- the model writes a placeholder engine that
doesn't capture lp85's click dynamics; [1] L2 induction STILL proposer_failed despite the split fix
being correct in isolation (unit tests + isolated real-prompt test pass). Likely mechanism: the
combined + focused engine calls ramble to the 2560 limit on the real multi-transition prompt and
exceed the 300s proposer timeout (worsened by concurrent-conductor iGPU contention).

HONEST conclusion: truncation fix + goal-repair + split are each correct/necessary but NOT
sufficient -- the binding wall is that Qwen3.5-9B produces low-quality rambling/placeholder code on
the REAL lp85 prompts (12%-accurate engine, return-False goal), which the synthetic prompts masked.
A model-capability / induction-quality wall, not prompt engineering. Revised lever: the
perception-grounded structural-alignment goal (less for the model to induce) + the engine-accuracy
problem (structured action-effect model) + possibly a stronger offline inducer. Budget bump and split
are confirmed insufficient alone. The split-fallback stays shipped (real robustness improvement).

